    "body": "Audit passed: OK to merge and deploy\n\nExact-head application audit of PR #294 by Claudio. This is the one-time exception PR for the native-workbench import fix.\n\n- **Head:** 5e65fe5b587747efc717f167f9b61469effa9afe\n- **Tree:** 336223df0161caeae4eb7db1e40df748d8ba110f\n- **Base:** 5dd5488d138514351fffd54d0b0232ae19fcb64d, which is still current main.\n\nWhat I checked:\n- **PR CI:** \"Test & Build\" run 38247731718 is SUCCESS on this exact head.\n- **My own full Linux server run at this head:** 360/360 suites and 5478/5478 tests passed, with no filter, in 4064.9 s.\n- **Client:** the build passes, and lint shows 0 errors and 14 warnings, all pre-existing.\n- **Focused install suite:** 100/100 passed.\n- **Diff review.** Five files changed:\n  - `post205-draft-tables.json` adds the closed historical `preNativeWorkbench` and `postNativeWorkbench` pair. The six existing variants are byte-identical.\n  - `instrumentImportMigrationSource.js` updates the SHA and the key list.\n  - `instrumentImportSchemaService.js` accepts the pair only in the preDraft and upgradedDraft lists.\n  - The `workflowWriteScanner.js` loader hash is updated.\n  - The install test covers the native fixture for both Prisma and native workbench, plus 4 nearby-variant refusals.\n  - The change is additive. No migration, row or constraint is altered, and there is no hard-coded lab policy.\n- **Schema hashes:** I independently reproduced the native SQL from `migrate_workbench_drafts.js` plus the #205 records ALTER.\n  - The pre hash is e3c04c14115c007fb7a5ff84f32b7f3e9adb22c178746f7f13c8ed0bd45e9e67.\n  - After the #200 importReceiptId ALTER, the post hash is 4e6096cd9a8de0b71181392944f8776cad44d24041d0e4b181e881120151297c.\n  - These match the failed proof's retained schema.\n- **Unicode test strings** were restored correctly at this head.\n\nThis approves the application merge only. Production still needs:\n- a NEW proof-source review bound to the actual merge, this audit and an exact first proof root;\n- the first isolated proof;\n- a NEW production-source review;\n- an exact-kit audit;\n- one fresh single-use gate.\n\nThe failed proof root from 10:52Z stays sealed. Other application merges stay held until #200 is live and post-checked.\n\nRefs #200\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
